  "hypothesis": "An MLP block at 4096 tokens with hidden 7168 stores its gate and up projections in one [4096, 14336] bf16 buffer. The shipped path computes F.silu(x[:, :7168]) * x[:, 7168:], which launches two kernels, writes the 58.7 MB silu output back to HBM only to read it again, and walks both inputs as non-contiguous views. A single fused kernel that reads the 117.4 MB buffer once and writes 58.7 MB is claimed to recover most of the measured gap to a kernel that moves the same bytes.\n",
  "mechanism": {
    "name": "one fused silu_and_mul pass over the interleaved gate/up buffer",
    "class": "fusion",
    "justification": "torch.add(a, b) moves exactly the fused kernel's bytes with the same contiguous access pattern and finishes in 0.05310 ms, so the missing time is addressable, not a property of the workload. The output is bit-identical: silu and mul are elementwise.\n"
  },
